  "milestones": [
    {
      "id": "m1",
      "title": "m1: fix truncate length guarantee",
      "status": "done",
      "plan": "Fix truncate in src/text.js so the returned string is never longer than max. When truncation is needed the result ends with \"...\" and the ellipsis counts toward max: slice to max-3 then append. Edge case max < 3: return text.slice(0, max) so the length bound still holds. Do not change capitalize or the short-text early return.\n\nAdd a regression test in test/ covering: length <= max for a long string, suffix \"...\" when cut, unchanged short text and capitalize. Run npm test.\n\nAcceptance: length bound holds for max values including 3 and below, ellipsis only on cut, existing tests still pass, dev server / renders soak.",
      "preview": {
        "route": "/"
      },
